@local/dsh-prompt-forecast README · Prompt Forecast：English | [中文](README.zh.md)

Ghost-text prediction of your next action in the DeepSeek Harness Web composer,
in the style of Codex and Claude Code prompt suggestions.

@local/dsh-prompt-forecast README · Prompt Forecast：The default mode is a Codex-style context fork: the parent's current text
transcript plus one synthetic user turn, `Suggest my next message.`, with
explicit rules that restrict the answer to an action.

@local/dsh-prompt-forecast README · What gets predicted：The target is the next **actionable** message, not a literal continuation of the
conversation. A useful suggestion is one the user would send to tell the
assistant what to do next:

@local/dsh-prompt-forecast README · From a local checkout：Use Plugin Manager with this package directory as the bundle target. The bundle
patch inserts the `prompt-forecast` row; it survives restarts because it is a
normal profile bundle.
